\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Remark}
\title{Alignment criteria across different training routes}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{alignment}

\p{Ouyang et al. combine demonstrations, comparison-trained rewards, and PPO
in \citet{Sections 3.1--3.5}{ouyang2022training}. Direct Preference
Optimization replaces the learned-reward PPO stage with a preference loss in
\citet{Section 4}{rafailov2023direct}. The broader alignment-training
description is a proposed way to compare such routes; it does not identify
their observations or objectives with one another.}

\p{The declared behavioral criterion is part of the claim, while the
independent evaluation remains a separate object. Their agreement is an
empirical or theoretical claim, not a consequence of the word alignment.}
